    "message": "feat(daemon): widen opening-narrative budget and retry past the deadline\n\nRoot cause (source-live attempts D/E): GPT-5 counts hidden reasoning against\nmax_completion_tokens, so the 320-token narrator budget routinely burned out\nbefore any visible text, and the 60s deadline class was never retried.\n\n- MAX_ACTION_NARRATIVE_TOKENS 320 -> 1024: leaves room for reasoning to\n  finish AND a genuine 1-2 sentence public note (responsiveness stays bounded\n  by the route narrative deadline).\n- Corrective re-prompt now also fires when the opening exceeds\n  OPENING_NARRATIVE_DEADLINE_MS, not only on empty/error completions. A\n  generation guard (currentNarrativeAttempt) ensures a superseded stream's\n  late events never leak to the SSE writer; per-attempt instrumentation logs\n  the reason at \"opening narrative attempt failed\".\n- Narrator system prompt: begin the visible note on the very first output\n  token; the note is the deliverable, not a summary of a longer draft.\n\nTests: core chatPublicOpening 10/10 (maxTokens 1024); daemon gate suite 4/4\nincl. new deadline-retry case (injected 80ms deadline, blocked-then-text\nstream, exactly one corrective re-prompt, no turn.failed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  },
